{"id":3081,"date":"2025-11-30T21:47:15","date_gmt":"2025-11-30T21:47:15","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/shopcardboardboxes.com\/?post_type=product&#038;p=3081"},"modified":"2026-02-14T22:48:27","modified_gmt":"2026-02-14T22:48:27","slug":"cardboard-catering-trays","status":"publish","type":"product","link":"https:\/\/shopcardboardboxes.com\/product\/cardboard-catering-trays\/","title":{"rendered":"Cardboard Catering Trays"},"content":{"rendered":"<h2>Cardboard Catering Trays For Food Sellers<\/h2>\n<p>Catering setups require strong, steady, and well-shaped trays that hold assorted food items without bending. Many catering teams already pack chilled meals and salads in <a href=\"https:\/\/shopcardboardboxes.com\/product\/cardboard-meal-prep-boxes\/\"><strong>Cardboard Meal Prep Boxes<\/strong><\/a>, so they plan their catering trays to work alongside those boxes for coordinated food packing and presentation. Cardboard catering trays provide stability when staff moves food from preparation areas to service counters and self-serve stations. These trays help keep items arranged, limit spills, and keep the serving layout neat during busy hours.<\/p>\n<p>These trays work with sandwiches, rolls, pastries, tarts, muffins, wraps, desserts, and cold servings. The wide tray surface allows neat food placement, while the raised edges help reduce slipping when trays are carried. With cardboard catering trays wholesale, restaurants can manage bulk orders for large events while keeping sizes and tray formats consistent. These trays support loading and serving while keeping items grouped and easy to identify.<\/p>\n<h3><strong>How Catering Trays Support Organized Serving<\/strong><\/h3>\n<p>Organized serving becomes easier when trays keep items aligned and separated.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Key Handling Points<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Helps maintain neat food arrangement<\/li>\n<li>Limits sliding when trays are moved<\/li>\n<li>Supports assorted servings without mixing<\/li>\n<li>Supports handling for staff during service<\/li>\n<li>Reduces food movement during transport<\/li>\n<li>Keeps table displays arranged and readable<\/li>\n<li>Helps serve multiple items together on one tray<\/li>\n<li>Reduces preparation time in busy kitchens<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<table style=\"height: 224px;\" width=\"910\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Type<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Material<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Wall Strength<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Best Use<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Finish<\/strong><\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Flat catering tray<\/td>\n<td>Kraft board<\/td>\n<td>Medium<\/td>\n<td>Sandwich sets<\/td>\n<td>Matte<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deep catering tray<\/td>\n<td>Rigid card<\/td>\n<td>Strong<\/td>\n<td>Heavy snacks<\/td>\n<td>Smooth<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wide serving tray<\/td>\n<td>Cardboard<\/td>\n<td>Standard<\/td>\n<td>Pastries &amp; sweets<\/td>\n<td>Semi-gloss<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi-item tray<\/td>\n<td>Corrugated<\/td>\n<td>High<\/td>\n<td>Group servings<\/td>\n<td>Natural<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<h2>Large Cardboard Catering Trays For Big Orders<\/h2>\n<p>Large cardboard catering trays are used when restaurants, bakeries, or caterers need extra serving space for multiple items. Many event sellers match tray choices with ranges named <a href=\"https:\/\/shopcardboardboxes.com\/product-category\/food-related-cardboard-boxes\/\"><strong>Food Related Cardboard Boxes<\/strong><\/a>, so serving trays and packaging boxes follow similar sizes and layouts during full event service. Large trays help teams arrange long sandwich rows, assorted pastries, mixed snacks, and bulk servings prepared within short time windows.<\/p>\n<p>These trays support both hot and cold items. Their broad base helps keep items in place when arranged in rows or sections. They can hold cup dividers, snack holders, and small inserts for mixed food types. When staff moves between the kitchen and event tables, these trays help keep items steady and easier to carry.<\/p>\n<h3><strong>Why Large Catering Trays Are Important<\/strong><\/h3>\n<p>Large trays are used for events where food is displayed in longer, continuous layouts.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Bulk Serving Points<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Holds more quantity on a single tray<\/li>\n<li>Keeps arranged sections neat and readable<\/li>\n<li>Helps manage event serving flow<\/li>\n<li>Supports multi-item serving across courses<\/li>\n<li>Works well for buffet lines and counters<\/li>\n<li>Helps arrange items in rows and groups<\/li>\n<li>Reduces bending under heavier loads<\/li>\n<li>Supports bulk preparation and service<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Size<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Capacity<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Board Type<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Edge Height<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Common Setting<\/strong><\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Medium<\/td>\n<td>Assorted items<\/td>\n<td>Kraft<\/td>\n<td>Low edge<\/td>\n<td>Corporate events<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Large<\/td>\n<td>Multiple servings<\/td>\n<td>Rigid card<\/td>\n<td>High edge<\/td>\n<td>Parties<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>XL wide<\/td>\n<td>Heavy food<\/td>\n<td>Corrugated<\/td>\n<td>Medium edge<\/td>\n<td>Catering stations<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slim long<\/td>\n<td>Sandwich rows<\/td>\n<td>Cardboard<\/td>\n<td>Low edge<\/td>\n<td>Caf\u00e9 platters<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<h2>Cardboard Catering Trays With Lids For Clean Handling<\/h2>\n<p>Cardboard catering trays with lids add coverage when food needs to be moved quickly or held for a short time before serving. These lid-based trays help limit dust contact, support short holding periods, and allow safer stacking during peak hours. Many restaurants keep lid-style trays aligned with serving ranges titled <a href=\"https:\/\/shopcardboardboxes.com\/\"><strong>Cardboard Boxes for Packaging<\/strong><\/a>, so colors, branding, and print themes remain consistent across food service and takeaway lines.<\/p>\n<p>Lid designs help reduce drying for pastries, limit exposure for sandwich tops, and cover fruits and snacks during transport. These trays help keep items in the same arrangement during travel and keep the tray layout intact until serving time. Lid-style trays also help when staff needs to label contents on the top surface for quick identification.<\/p>\n<h3><strong>Why Lid-Style Trays Help During Events<\/strong><\/h3>\n<p>Lid-based trays reduce exposure and support covered serving layouts.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Covered Transport Points<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Limits dust contact during transport<\/li>\n<li>Supports stacking in delivery vehicles<\/li>\n<li>Helps maintain condition for short holding times<\/li>\n<li>Supports off-site catering and event delivery<\/li>\n<li>Allows labeling on lids for quick checks<\/li>\n<li>Helps protect delicate items during movement<\/li>\n<li>Reduces accidental contact and smudging<\/li>\n<li>Keeps food arranged until serving time<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Lid Type<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Material<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Strength<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Best Use<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Surface Style<\/strong><\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Full lid<\/td>\n<td>Solid cardboard<\/td>\n<td>Strong<\/td>\n<td>Sandwich trays<\/td>\n<td>Gloss<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Shallow lid<\/td>\n<td>Kraft<\/td>\n<td>Medium<\/td>\n<td>Pastry sets<\/td>\n<td>Matte<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Window lid<\/td>\n<td>SBS<\/td>\n<td>Firm<\/td>\n<td>Assorted snacks<\/td>\n<td>Smooth<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deep lid<\/td>\n<td>Rigid card<\/td>\n<td>Very strong<\/td>\n<td>Mixed foods<\/td>\n<td>Natural matte<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<h2>Cardboard Trays With Handles For Easy Carrying<\/h2>\n<p>Cardboard trays with handles help staff move heavy or multi-item servings with more control. These handled trays are used during corporate events, school functions, bakery rush orders, and caf\u00e9 service where movement between counters and seating areas is frequent. The handle area is shaped to support weight more evenly so the tray is less likely to tilt while being carried.<\/p>\n<p>Handle-based trays provide a defined grip point for movement. The added grip area helps reduce slipping when the tray holds many items or heavier products. These trays are useful when staff carries trays over longer distances, such as across halls, outdoor venues, or large dining areas.<\/p>\n<h3><strong>Why Handle Trays Improve Service<\/strong><\/h3>\n<p>Handle trays reduce strain and help keep items steady during carrying.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Carrying Control Points<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Provides grip for frequent service routes<\/li>\n<li>Supports controlled movement while walking<\/li>\n<li>Useful for multi-item platters and trays<\/li>\n<li>Supports longer carry distances at events<\/li>\n<li>Reduces tilting under load<\/li>\n<li>Supports steadier handling during movement<\/li>\n<li>Helps with repeat trips during larger events<\/li>\n<li>Supports staff carrying prepared trays<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<table style=\"height: 245px;\" width=\"875\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Handle Type<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Grip Level<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Material<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Best Food Type<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Finish<\/strong><\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Side handle<\/td>\n<td>Strong<\/td>\n<td>Kraft<\/td>\n<td>Pastries<\/td>\n<td>Matte<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Top-cut handle<\/td>\n<td>Secure<\/td>\n<td>Cardboard<\/td>\n<td>Sandwiches<\/td>\n<td>Smooth<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Folded handle<\/td>\n<td>Medium<\/td>\n<td>Rigid board<\/td>\n<td>Snacks<\/td>\n<td>Natural<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dual-slot handle<\/td>\n<td>High<\/td>\n<td>Corrugated<\/td>\n<td>Heavy items<\/td>\n<td>Semi-gloss<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<h2>Cardboard Tray With Dividers For Organized Sections<\/h2>\n<p>Cardboard trays with dividers help businesses separate food types inside the same tray. Dividers keep fruits, pastries, sandwiches, and snacks in their own sections so shapes and placements remain clear. This supports readable layout for guests and helps staff confirm items at a glance. Dividers also limit movement during transport when trays are carried or stacked.<\/p>\n<p>These trays help event handling because staff can arrange mixed items inside one tray without mixing or sliding. Dividers may be removable or fixed depending on the serving requirement, which allows menu changes without changing the full tray format. One tray can hold sweet items on one side and savory items on the other without contact.<\/p>\n<h3><strong>Why Dividers Support Mixed Food Arrangements<\/strong><\/h3>\n<p>Dividers help keep assorted food items separated within one tray.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Section Control Points<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Separates food groups within one tray<\/li>\n<li>Limits contact between different items<\/li>\n<li>Keeps layout clear and easy to read<\/li>\n<li>Supports assorted servings in shared platters<\/li>\n<li>Helps organize items for faster service<\/li>\n<li>Makes serving easier during events<\/li>\n<li>Reduces mixing between sweet and savory items<\/li>\n<li>Supports structured catering tray layouts<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<table style=\"height: 239px;\" width=\"927\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Divider Type<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Slot Count<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Material<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Depth<\/strong><\/th>\n<th><strong>Ideal Use<\/strong><\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Fixed dividers<\/td>\n<td>3\u20134 slots<\/td>\n<td>Strong card<\/td>\n<td>Deep<\/td>\n<td>Pastries<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Removable dividers<\/td>\n<td>Variable slots<\/td>\n<td>Kraft<\/td>\n<td>Standard<\/td>\n<td>Mixed snacks<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Grid layout<\/td>\n<td>Multi-section<\/td>\n<td>SBS<\/td>\n<td>Medium<\/td>\n<td>Events<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Long divider<\/td>\n<td>2 rows<\/td>\n<td>Corrugated<\/td>\n<td>High<\/td>\n<td>Sandwiches<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Cardboard catering trays help restaurants, bakeries, and food service teams organize meals in clean layouts with strong base support and well-shaped walls. In the second line, many food sellers rely on <strong data-start=\"1972\" data-end=\"2031\">Shop Cardboard Boxes<\/strong> to get customized catering trays that match event themes and daily serving needs.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":4513,"template":"","meta":{"_joinchat":[]},"product_brand":[],"product_cat":[183],"product_tag":[],"class_list":["post-3081","product","type-product","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","product_cat-food-related-cardboard-boxes","rishi-post","first","instock","shipping-taxable","purchasable","product-type-simple"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v27.9 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>Cardboard Catering Trays Wholesale | SCB<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"High-quality cardboard catering trays wholesale at SCB. Custom sizes, food-safe materials, fast shipping, and printing options for all catering needs.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/shopcardboardboxes.com\/product\/cardboard-catering-trays\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Cardboard Catering Trays Wholesale | SCB\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"High-quality cardboard catering trays wholesale at SCB. Custom sizes, food-safe materials, fast shipping, and printing options for all catering needs.\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/shopcardboardboxes.com\/product\/cardboard-catering-trays\/\" \/>\n<m